  "authorNotes": "Book: the 2026 'আমার বাংলা বই' (Class 1) PDF from Downloads/Board Book and TG 2026/Book/Class 1 Bangla.pdf; I read pages 30–80 (পাঠ ২১–৫৪) as images, so every bookRef is a real page. Reused from MP Annual 2026: word meanings (6 of its 10), sentence-making words (all 5), letters for row 5 (5, changed from '2 words' to '1 word + 1 sentence'), antonyms (5 of its 8; skipped 'আয়' because in 'মামার বাড়ি' it means 'come', not income), all 5 fill-in-the-blanks, 5 of 6 short questions, and its 'আমাদের দেশ' paragraph turned into a word-bank 5-sentence task. MP 2026's conjunct row asked children to BREAK the conjunct, which the Sylhet rule forbids, so row 7 asks only for 2 words; of its conjuncts only প্ত is in pp30–80 (ন্ত and ন্ধ are not taught there), the other three come from MP 2025 / HY 2026 and all appear in the book. MP 2026 had no matching, MCQ, কারচিহ্ন or table rows: matching is the book's own p69 exercise, MCQs are new from the book (one adapted from MP 2025), কারচিহ্ন takes 3 from MP HY 2026 + 2 new. Row 11 (vocabulary) = six seasons + four directions, both taken verbatim from MP HY 2026 — the label also allows 'অন্যান্য', so the 12 Bangla months (MP 2026 Q4, book p75) could replace them if the owner prefers. Row 12 table = number-spelling table modelled on the book's p76 exercise. Doubts: (1) no duration was published — I used 2 hours like MP; (2) row 5 includes ণ (from MP), which children can only use mid-word (হরিণ, লবণ) — the answer key says that is acceptable; (3) row 13 item 2 needs a picture (river, boat, trees, birds) added by the Office. MP HY 2026 items on রাখাল/ডালিম/টগর were not used — they are before পাঠ ২১."
